- examined management’s judgements and assessments in
respect of whether provisions are required;
- considered the management assessments of those matters
that are not disclosed as contingent liability since the
probability of material outflow is considered to be remote;
- reviewed the adequacy and completeness of disclosures;
Based on the above procedures performed, the estimation and
disclosures of contingent liabilities are considered to be
adequate and reasonable.
